    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced `getMembershipTier()` (which returned `GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) with `getMembershipLevel()`: starts at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3. The old GOLD/household-size logic is gone (level 4 is reserved for tenure).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed the `membershipTier` string property from the Owner response schema and added `membershipLevel` (integer, 1\u20133). Since the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, the response now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer `membershipTier`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Updated the create audit line to record `membershipLevel={}` instead of nothing tier-related.\n\nAll existing and new tests are green (34 passed), including the membership-specific ones: Cp15 (numeric level replaces tier), Cp21 (audit records the level), Cp23 (GOLD gone \u2192 household member is level 2), and Cp24 (capped at 3).",
